2: title: Collection of biostratigraphic data from petroleum wells (known as STRATDAT database)
3: summary: >-
4:   "Geoscience Australia's biostratigraphic database (STRADAT) provides information about the
5:   biozonation of sedimentary rocks that were intersected by offshore petroleum wells." Data come
6:   from well completion reports and destructive analyses reports submitted under the OPGGSA 2006 and
7:   the PSLA 1967, and from GA, AGSO, BMR and state studies.
8: publisher: {name: Geoscience Australia, url: https://www.ga.gov.au, country: AU}
9: origin:
10:   url: https://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/146442
11:   access: anonymous
12:   notes: "eCat 10ac40b7-844c-4ea2-bd84-23eaadfa4e77, DOI 10.26186/146442. Served as layer resfacs:Biostratigraphy of the WFS https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/resfacs/ows and through https://portal.ga.gov.au/. No manifest_url: the data are a web feature service and a portal, with no file listing the verifier reads."
13: licence:
14:   name: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International Licence
15:   spdx: CC-BY-4.0
16:   url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
17:   redistribution: allowed
18:   attribution: required
19: kinds: [tops]
20: region: {country: AU, basin: Australian offshore basins, bbox: [110.0, -45.0, 155.0, -5.0]}
21: listed_by: [publisher]
22: known_issues:
23:   - "bbox is the WFS capabilities WGS84BoundingBox of resfacs:Biostratigraphy; the eCat record states no extent."
24:   - "Biozone picks by depth, recorded under the 'tops' kind."
25: notes: "No period stated: the eCat record gives creation 2022-03-31 and publication 2022-03-08 only."
26: added: 2026-10-24


